There is a possibility of commit failure if the selected pipe/output
won't support Bigjoiner or 8K. So we need to handle this case.

Signed-off-by: Bhanuprakash Modem <bhanuprakash.modem@intel.com>
---
 lib/igt_kms.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/igt_kms.c b/lib/igt_kms.c
index e1a65244..0e8c6f1d 100644
--- a/lib/igt_kms.c
+++ b/lib/igt_kms.c
@@ -5692,6 +5692,10 @@ bool igt_max_bpc_constraint(igt_display_t *display, enum pipe pipe,
 
 	for_each_connector_mode(output) {
 		igt_output_override_mode(output, &connector->modes[j__]);
+
+		if (!igt_check_bigjoiner_support(display))
+			continue;
+
 		igt_display_commit2(display, display->is_atomic ? COMMIT_ATOMIC : COMMIT_LEGACY);
 
 		if (!igt_check_output_bpc_equal(display->drm_fd, pipe,
